               MIT plus upstream third-party notices, Copyright 2026 Chan
               Zuckerberg Biohub, Inc.
               -> src/foldjax/models/esmfold2/{LICENSE,NOTICE}
               Chemistry tables derived from Transformers' Apache-2.0
               ESMFold2 support are identified in that NOTICE.

  OpenDDE      https://huggingface.co/aurekaresearch/OpenDDE
               Apache-2.0
               -> src/foldjax/models/opendde/{LICENSE,NOTICE}

  OpenFold3    https://github.com/aqlaboratory/openfold-3
               Apache-2.0, Copyright the OpenFold Team
               -> src/foldjax/models/openfold3/{LICENSE,NOTICE}
               Two things are carried under this one upstream. The JAX port is
               a reimplementation; `models/openfold3/_upstream/` additionally
               contains upstream's own *data pipeline*, vendored verbatim
               (~46k lines) so featurization needs no separate checkout. That
               tree is upstream's code under upstream's licence, kept in
               upstream's style so it stays diffable against the repository it
               came from; the single edit is marked in
               `core/data/framework/__init__.py`.

  Protenix     https://github.com/bytedance/Protenix
               Apache-2.0, Copyright 2024 ByteDance and/or its affiliates
